# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""
dnaplay  -  "Base Pair Binder", a terminal game for the genomics server.

A DNA duplex scrolls in opposite directions near the top and bottom of the
screen. Pilot a short PRIMER (3-5 bases) through the field and fly into the
matching strand to bind.

    ARROWS/WASD steer   SPACE thrust   1 Helicase   2 Polymerase   P pause   Q quit

Scoring: you start at 100. A correct impact scores 3 per G-C pair and 2 per
A-T pair (their real hydrogen-bond counts) times your combo. A wrong impact
costs 5; a site that escapes costs 15 (double if mutated). Score <= 0 ends
the game and your PEAK score goes on the board.
The strand speeds up as you score and slows down again when you slip.

Every 3 bases you bind form a codon -> an amino acid.  A stop codon (TAA, TAG,
TGA) releases the protein for a bonus.

Options:  --daily     today's shared challenge strand
          --scores    print the scoreboard and exit
          --tutorial  show the tutorial first

Scores:   /var/lib/genomics-game/scores.log  (override with DNAPLAY_DIR)
Python 3 standard library only.  Never needs root.
"""
